    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0950" n="826" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg826"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.73/582: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-26T14:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 26—12:13
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>152. My 149, February 26, 11 a.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d770-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    acknowledges receipt of my two communications addressed to F. J. Brown<anchor
                        n="31" xml:id="d770-f2"/> with regard to the utilization of the joint
                    Western and Western Union cable between Brazil and the United States and adds:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Western Telegraph Company having carried out their part of the
                            agreement between the two companies, His Majesty’s Government are of
                            opinion that any proposal for the modification of that agreement should
                            be addressed to the Western Telegraph Company by the Western Union
                            Company direct.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d770-f1" n="30" xml:id="d770-f1-content">
